What is a Robotic Total Station?
A robotic total station is an advanced surveying instrument that integrates motorized servo drives, automated target recognition (ATR), and onboard data processing to perform precise angular and distance measurements without requiring a second operator at the instrument. These systems combine electronic theodolite functionality with electromagnetic distance measurement (EDM) technology, enabling a single surveyor to carry out complex topographic, construction layout, and monitoring tasks with significantly improved efficiency and accuracy.
